course: dictionary
lesson: 10612
title: Unemployed and what it means
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Unemployed means not having a paid job, even though you are able to work and want one. The prefix un- means not, and employed means having a job, so unemployed is the opposite of employed. «One town might have 8 in 100 unemployed.» That means 8 out of every 100 people there have no paid job.
explain: The unemployed means all the people without jobs. When you see «unemployed» before a noun, like «unemployed parents», it describes the people. Check the clues around it: a sentence about looking for work or getting help while searching tells you the word means no job.
explain: Other words can mean the same thing. «Between jobs» means unemployed, and «jobseeker» is an official UK word for an unemployed person. «In transition» can mean unemployed or changing jobs, so the context must decide which one the writer means.
fact: Unemployed means not having a paid job, though able and wanting to work.
fact: The unemployed means all the people without jobs.
fact: The prefix un- means not, so unemployed means not employed.
fact: «Between jobs» and «jobseeker» are other ways to say unemployed.
fact: «In transition» can mean unemployed or changing jobs, so check the context.
exercise: «One town might have 8 in 100 unemployed.» What does unemployed mean here? | People who work very hard every day | People who live in the town | *People without a paid job
exercise: Which phrase means the same as unemployed? | Working late every night | *Between jobs | On holiday in the sun | Full of energy
exercise: Jayden asks, «What does the unemployed mean?» | A new kind of job | *All the people without jobs | Only people who work in offices | Children who go to school
test: «While a parent is unemployed the family may claim benefits and cut spending.» Who is unemployed in this sentence? | A child who is ill at home | A neighbour who runs a shop | A grandparent who has retired | *A parent without a paid job
test: In the UK, which official word means an unemployed person looking for work? | Shopkeeper | *Jobseeker | Teacher | Pensioner
exam: Which word is the opposite of unemployed? | *Employed | Unkind | Unsure | Unwell
